<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50122" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱεροφάντ-ης</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱρ-</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαίνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hierophant, one
				who teaches rites of sacrifice and worship</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. τῶν χθονίων θεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.153
				</span></i>
			; of <i>the initiating priest</i> at Eleusis, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.76.24
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				6.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				7.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				33
			</span></i>; at Rome,= <i>pontifex</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.73
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.36
			</span></i>; of the <i>pontifex maximus</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Num.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; of the Jewish High Priest, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.322
			</span></i>; of <i><span class="en">
				Moses
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.117
			</span></i>; later, <i>mystical expounder</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. τῆς τετρακτύος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					20p.466M.
				</span></i>
			</div>
